.TH ATERMINAL 1 "2026-11-06" "aterminal @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aterminal \- phosphor CRT terminal emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aterminal
.RB [ \-\-green | \-\-amber ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-sound | \-\-sound ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-crt ]
.RB [ \-\-bitmap ]
.br
.RB [ \-\-size
.IR WIDTH x HEIGHT ]
.RB [ \-\-width
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-height
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-text\-size
.IR N ]
.br
.RB [ \-\-colour
.BR green | amber | colour ]
.RB [ \-\-fullscreen [ =true | =false ]| \-\-windowed ]
.br
.RB [ \-\-shell
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-e
.IR command ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR command ]
.RB [ \-\-demo ]
.RB [ \-\-motd [ =\fINAME\fR]]
.RB [ \-\-prompt
.IR style ]
.br
.RB [ \-\-geometry
.IR COLUMNS x ROWS ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-\-title
.IR text ]
.RB [ \-\-maximized ]
.RB [ \-\-console
.IR N ]
.br
.RB [ \-\-scrollback
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-l ]
.RB [ \-\-hold ]
.RB [ \-\-cursor
.IR style ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-blink ]
.br
.RB [ \-\-scanlines
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-bloom
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-bell
.IR mode ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.br
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-\-
.IR "program args..." ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aterminal
is a native Linux terminal with the look of a phosphor CRT: green or amber
text or a colour tube, soft bloom, scanlines, a vignette, and optional AdLib\-style key sounds.
.PP
Twelve independent shell consoles live behind the F1\-F12 keys. Each one starts
its own pseudo\-terminal when first visited and keeps running in the background.
.PP
.B aterminal
implements a practical VT100/ANSI subset with Unicode extensions, not complete
xterm compatibility. See
.B BUGS
before using it with applications that depend on advanced terminal features.
.PP
The window title shows the console and its size in characters, such as
.BR "aterminal / F1 / 80x25" .
.SH OPTIONS
Options that take a value accept either
.BI \-\-flag= value
or
.BI \-\-flag " value\fR."
Command\-line choices override saved preferences. If a setting appears more
than once, the last one wins.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show flags and keyboard shortcuts, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-size " WIDTH" x HEIGHT
Set the initial window size in pixels. The default fits 80x25 characters at the
text size in use.
.TP
.BI \-\-geometry " COLUMNS" x ROWS
Set the initial size in characters, 20\-500 by 5\-200. It cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-size ,
.BR \-\-width ,
or
.BR \-\-height .
.TP
.BI \-\-width " N\fR, " \-\-height " N"
Set the dimensions separately. Width is 400\-4096 and height is 280\-2160.
.TP
.BI \-\-text\-size " N"
Set the initial zoom level, 1\-6. The default is 6, lowered if needed to fit the
screen.
.TP
.BR \-\-colour " " green | amber | colour ", " \-\-color " " ...
Choose green or amber phosphor, or a colour CRT that shows ANSI, 256\-colour and
truecolour values in colour.
.TP
.BR \-\-green ", " \-\-amber
Short aliases for
.BR \-\-colour .
.TP
.BR \-\-fullscreen [ =true | =false | =1 | =0 ]
Start in desktop fullscreen, or windowed if the value is false.
.TP
.B \-\-windowed
Start windowed.
.TP
.B \-\-maximized
Start maximised.
.TP
.BI \-\-title " text"
Replace
.B aterminal
in the window title.
.TP
.BI \-\-console " N"
Open on console
.IR N ,
1\-12.
.TP
.BR \-\-sound ", " \-\-no\-sound
Enable or disable synthesized key clicks.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-crt
Disable bloom, scanlines, and the vignette.
.TP
.BI \-\-scanlines " N\fR, " \-\-bloom " N"
Set the strength of each effect, 0\-100 percent. The default is 100.
.TP
.BR \-\-cursor " " block | bar | underline
Choose the cursor shape.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-blink
Keep the cursor steady.
.TP
.BR \-\-bell " " visual | audible | none
Flash the screen, play a key click, or ignore the bell. The default is visual.
.TP
.BI \-\-scrollback " N"
Keep
.I N
history lines per console, 0\-1000000. The default is 10000.
.TP
.B \-\-bitmap
Use bitmap glyphs throughout instead of the mixed retro font.
.TP
.BI \-\-shell " path"
Select the shell executable. The path must be absolute.
.TP
.BI \-e " command\fR, " \-\-command " command"
Run
.I command
in the selected shell using
.BR \-c .
Quote it as one argument. Newly opened consoles run it too.
.TP
.BI \-c " command\fR, " \-\-startup " command"
Run
.I command
at startup, then continue in an interactive shell. It runs once, in the first
console only, and cannot be combined with
.B \-e
or
.BR \-\-demo .
Under bash it runs after
.IR ~/.bashrc ,
so aliases work. Other shells run it before their startup files.
.TP
.BI \-\- " program args..."
Run a program directly in every console, without a shell. This must come last.
.TP
.BI \-d " dir\fR, " \-\-working\-directory " dir"
Start consoles in
.IR dir .
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-login
Start a login shell.
.TP
.B \-\-hold
Keep a console open when its process ends, showing the exit status. Without it,
the console closes, and closing the last console quits
.BR aterminal .
A command that could not run, with status 126 or 127, always stays open.
.TP
.BI \-\-prompt " style"
Choose the bash prompt. The default is
.BR redhat .
The styles are
.BR slackware ,
.BR debian ,
.BR redhat ,
.BR bsd ,
.BR sunos ,
.BR unix ,
.BR bourne ,
.BR bash ,
and
.BR dos ,
or
.B none
to keep the prompt from your startup files.
.B \-\-prompt=list
shows them. Text containing a symbol or space, such as
.BR \-\-prompt=\(aq$\(aq ,
is used as the prompt itself.
.I ~/.bashrc
still runs. This needs an interactive bash shell.
.TP
.BR \-\-motd [ =\fINAME\fR]
Show a message of the day on each new console. With no name, or with
.BR random ,
each console picks at random.
.B \-\-motd=list
shows the names. This cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-demo .
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Read options from
.IR file ,
one per line without the leading dashes, as
.IR "name value" ,
.IR name = value ,
or
.IR name .
Blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
are ignored. Later options override the file.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Display the built\-in font and terminal demonstration, then open a shell.
.TP
.B \-\-self\-test
Run the SDL interaction checks without loading or saving preferences.
.TP
.BI \-\-frames " N"
Exit after
.I N
event\-loop iterations, 1\-1000000. This is not a duration in seconds.
.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot " path"
Save the final rendered display as a PNG when the application exits.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B F1\-F12
Switch to that console, creating it on first use. These keys are not forwarded
to applications.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Alt+Plus\fR, \fBCtrl+Shift+Alt+Minus
Increase or decrease the text size.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+A\fR, \fBCtrl+Shift+G
Select amber or green phosphor.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+O
Toggle the colour CRT.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+S
Toggle key sounds.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+R
Toggle CRT effects.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+B
Toggle all\-bitmap font mode.
.TP
.B Alt+Enter\fR, \fBCtrl+Shift+F
Toggle fullscreen.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+P\fR, right click
Open or close terminal setup. Escape also closes it.
.TP
Mouse drag
Select text. A single click clears the selection.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Copy the selected text and clear the selection, or send an interrupt when
nothing is selected.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C
Copy the selected text without sending an interrupt.
.TP
.B Ctrl+V\fR, \fBCtrl+Shift+V\fR, \fBShift+Insert
Paste the clipboard.
.TP
Middle click
Paste the selected text, including text selected in other applications, or the
clipboard if nothing is selected.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z\fR, \fBCtrl+Y
Forward to the shell or application.
.TP
.B Shift+PageUp\fR, \fBShift+PageDown\fR, mouse wheel
Move through the scrollback.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Enter
Restart a console kept open after its process ended.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHELL
The shell to start, unless
.B \-\-shell
is given. If it is unset,
.B /bin/sh
is used.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for the preferences file.
.TP
.BR TERM ", " COLORTERM
Set to
.B xterm\-256color
and
.B truecolor
for child processes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ${XDG_DATA_HOME:\-$HOME/.local/share}/ross\-newman/aterminal/preferences
Display colour mode, sound, CRT effects, and font mode, saved on normal exit.
Remove this file while
.B aterminal
is closed to reset them.
.TP
.I share/aterminal/unifont.hex
Unicode font data, located relative to the installed executable.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
.TP
.B 1
An option was invalid, or startup failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.B aterminal \-\-colour=amber \-\-size=1280x800 \-\-text\-size=3
.B aterminal \-\-green \-\-fullscreen \-\-no\-sound
.B aterminal \-\-shell /bin/bash \-e htop
.B aterminal \-c 'cd ~/repos && git status'
.B aterminal \-\-colour=colour \-\-prompt=slackware \-\-geometry=132x43
.B aterminal \-d ~/repos \-\-title Build \-\- make test
.fi
.SH BUGS
.B aterminal
advertises
.B xterm\-256color
but does not implement every xterm sequence. Mouse reporting, sixel graphics,
OSC clipboard access, and DEC double\-height text are not
implemented. Emoji are monochrome, and complex\-script shaping and bidirectional
layout are not implemented.
.PP
Sessions are not restored across launches. Closing the window terminates its
shells.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR tmux (1),
.BR xterm (1)
